---
// ============================================================================
// LUSSARO BLOG — COMPARISON (three cars)
//
// Built from .claude/skills/blog/templates/comparison.astro. The template is
// two-car; this post compares all three Huracáns we run, so the frontmatter
// carries three cars and the spec table three columns. Everything outside the
// BODY region is the shared layout and is unchanged.
//
// ANGLE (owner, 15 Nov 2026): the post recommends the STO and makes it the
// primary call to action, while saying plainly where the EVO or the Spyder is
// the better fit — the cheaper-car honesty in references/voice.md still holds.
// ============================================================================

// KEYWORD CLUSTER — must match the entry in /used-keywords.md
//   PRIMARY:    lamborghini huracan sto vs evo rental miami
//   SECONDARY:  lamborghini huracan evo vs spyder rental miami,
//               huracan sto vs evo spyder, is the huracan sto awd or rwd,
//               is the huracan sto street legal,
//               how much is it to rent a lamborghini huracan for a day,
//               huracan sto vs evo, huracan sto deposit miami,
//               which lamborghini huracan to rent miami
//
// The commercial term "Lamborghini Huracán STO rental Miami" belongs to
// /cars/huracan-sto. This post is the comparison and funnels into that page.

import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '@/components/site/Nav.astro';
import CtaBand from '@/components/site/CtaBand.astro';
import StickyMobileCta from '@/components/site/StickyMobileCta.astro';
import RelatedPosts from '@/components/blog/RelatedPosts.astro';
import { altFor } from '@/data/image-alt';
import { cars } from '@/data/cars';
import { reviews } from '@/data/reviews';
import { business, telHref, whatsappWith, addressLine, hoursSummary } from '@/data/business';
import { rentalTerms, rateForDays } from '@/data/rental-terms';

const bySlug = (s) => cars.find((c) => c.slug === s);

const sto = bySlug('huracan-sto');
const evo = bySlug('huracan-evo');
const spyder = bySlug('huracan-evo-spyder');

const { mileage, insurance, cancellation, taxesAndFeesRate } = rentalTerms;
const perDay = mileage.includedPerDay;
const usd = (n) => `$${n.toLocaleString('en-US')}`;
const taxPct = Math.round(taxesAndFeesRate * 100);

const stoOverEvo = sto.price - evo.price;
const stoOverSpyder = sto.price - spyder.price;
const spyderOverEvo = spyder.price - evo.price;
const hpGap = sto.power - evo.power;
const threeDay = (c) => rateForDays(c.price, 3, c.discountTiers).perDay;   // .perDay — it returns an object
const week = (c) => rateForDays(c.price, 7, c.discountTiers).perDay;
// "Rear-wheel drive" from fleet.js, so the FAQ cannot drift from the spec.
const stoDrive = (sto.drivetrain || '').split(' · ')[0] || 'Rear-wheel drive';

const SITE = 'https://www.lussarocollection.com';
const SLUG = 'lamborghini-huracan-sto-vs-evo-rental-miami';
const PATH = `/blog/${SLUG}`;
const PAGE_URL = `${SITE}${PATH}`;

const HERO_KEY = '/cars/lamborghini-huracan-sto-rental-miami-front-quarter.jpg';
const heroSrc = `/blog/${SLUG}-hero-760.webp`;
const heroSrcSet = [560, 760, 800, 1120, 1200, 1560].map((w) => `/blog/${SLUG}-hero-${w}.webp ${w}w`).join(', ');
const heroAlt = altFor(HERO_KEY);

const BODY_KEY = '/cars/lamborghini-huracan-sto-rental-miami-side-profile.jpg';
const bodySrc = `/blog/${SLUG}-body-1000.webp`;
const bodySrcSet = `/blog/${SLUG}-body-700.webp 700w, /blog/${SLUG}-body-1000.webp 1000w`;
const bodyAlt = altFor(BODY_KEY);

const OG_IMAGE = `${SITE}/og/${SLUG}.jpg`;

const PUBLISHED_ISO = '2026-11-15';
const UPDATED_ISO = '2026-11-15';
const published = 'November 15, 2026';
const updated = 'November 15, 2026';
const readingMinutes = 8;

const TITLE = 'Huracán STO vs EVO Rental Miami: Which to Rent';
const DESCRIPTION = `Lamborghini Huracán STO vs EVO rental in Miami, plus the EVO Spyder: price, power, deposit and age side by side, and why the STO is the one we'd book.`;
const waMessage = "Hi, I read your Huracán STO vs EVO guide and I'd like to check dates for the STO.";
const wa = whatsappWith(waMessage, { car: `${sto.make} ${sto.name}`, page: PATH });

// Verbatim Google review that names a Lamborghini. No exclamation marks.
const testimonial = reviews.find((r) => r.name === 'Shaf Irfan');

const toc = [
  { id: 'what-they-share', label: 'What all three share' },
  { id: 'sto-vs-evo', label: 'What the STO adds over the EVO' },
  { id: 'evo-vs-spyder', label: 'EVO vs Spyder: the roof' },
  { id: 'when-not-the-sto', label: 'When the EVO or Spyder is right' },
  { id: 'terms', label: 'Deposit, age and mileage' },
  { id: 'our-pick', label: 'Why we would put you in the STO' },
  { id: 'faq', label: 'Common questions' },
];

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Is the Huracán STO faster than the Huracán EVO?',
    a: `On paper, yes. The STO makes ${sto.power} hp against the EVO's ${evo.power}, and Lamborghini quotes ${sto.zeroToSixty} to 60 for the STO against ${evo.zeroToSixty} for our EVO. Both drive the rear wheels only. The bigger difference on a Miami road is not the figure; it is how much more directly the STO responds.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Why is the deposit higher on the Huracán STO?',
    a: `The STO carries a ${sto.deposit.display} refundable deposit, against ${evo.deposit.display} on the EVO and the Spyder. It is the owner's figure for this car, taken when the booking is confirmed and returned after the car is inspected on return, the same way as every deposit we take.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'How old do you have to be to rent a Huracán STO in Miami?',
    a: `${sto.minimumAge}, with a valid license and qualifying insurance. The EVO and the EVO Spyder are ${evo.minimumAge}+, so a driver between those ages has two Huracáns to choose from rather than three.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Can the EVO Spyder roof open while driving?',
    a: `Yes, at low speed, so a passing shower does not mean pulling over. The rear window also lowers on its own, which lets you keep the roof up for the air conditioning and still hear the V10.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Is the Huracán STO AWD or RWD?',
    a: `${stoDrive}, like our Huracán EVO and EVO Spyder. All three send the V10's power to the rear wheels only, which is a large part of why they feel so alive on the road.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Is the Huracán STO street legal?',
    a: `Yes. STO stands for Super Trofeo Omologata, and omologata is Italian for homologated: approved for the road. It is the road-legal version of Lamborghini's one-make race car, registered for public roads like every car we rent.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'How much is it to rent a Lamborghini Huracán for a day in Miami?',
    a: `With us, ${usd(evo.price)} a day for the Huracán EVO, ${usd(spyder.price)} for the EVO Spyder and ${usd(sto.price)} for the Huracán STO, each with ${perDay} miles included. Longer bookings cost less per day: three days or more brings the STO to ${usd(threeDay(sto))} a day. Taxes and fees of ${taxPct}% are added to the rental.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Which Huracán is best for a photo or video shoot?',
    a: `The STO. The rear wing, the roof scoop and the livery read clearly on camera from every angle, and nothing else we run looks like it. The Spyder is the better choice only if the shot needs the roof down.`,
  },
];

// --- Schema. Do not restructure. ------------------------------------------
const authorSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Person',
  '@id': `${SITE}/about#robert`,
  name: 'Robert Comella',
  jobTitle: 'Founder',
  url: `${SITE}/about`,
  worksFor: { '@type': 'Organization', name: business.brandName, url: `${SITE}/` },
};

const articleSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: TITLE,
  description: DESCRIPTION,
  image: OG_IMAGE,
  datePublished: PUBLISHED_ISO,
  dateModified: UPDATED_ISO,
  author: { '@id': `${SITE}/about#robert` },
  publisher: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: business.brandName,
    logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: `${SITE}/favicon.png` },
  },
  mainEntityOfPage: { '@type': 'WebPage', '@id': PAGE_URL },
};

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: f.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a },
  })),
};

const mapLink = `https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=${encodeURIComponent(addressLine)}`;
---
<Layout
  title={`${TITLE} | Lussaro`}
  description={DESCRIPTION}
  image={OG_IMAGE}
  type="article"
  breadcrumbName="Huracán STO vs EVO"
  schema={[articleSchema, authorSchema, faqSchema]}
>
  {/* Skip link stays on the page, not in Layout: the other routes have no
       #main target yet, and a skip link that lands nowhere is worse than none. */}
  <a
    href="#main"
    class="sr-only focus:not-sr-only focus:fixed focus:top-4 focus:left-4 focus:z-[100] focus:bg-white focus:text-black focus:px-5 focus:py-3 focus:rounded-full focus:font-semibold focus:ring-2 focus:ring-[#ff1516]"
  >
    Skip to content
  </a>

  <Nav />

  <main id="main" tabindex="-1">
    {/* The header sits OUTSIDE <article> deliberately — see the template. */}
      <header class="bg-[#0a0a0a] pt-28 md:pt-32 pb-12 md:pb-16">
        <div class="max-w-[1140px] mx-auto px-5 md:px-8">
          <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-7">
            <ol class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center lg:justify-start gap-2 text-xs text-white/50">
              <li><a href="/" class="hover:text-white transition">Home</a></li>
              <li aria-hidden="true">/</li>
              <li><a href="/blog" class="hover:text-white transition">Rental Guides</a></li>
              <li aria-hidden="true">/</li>
              <li aria-current="page" class="text-white/70">Huracán STO vs EVO</li>
            </ol>
          </nav>

          <div class="lg:grid lg:grid-cols-[1.05fr_1fr] lg:gap-12 xl:gap-16">
            <div class="text-center lg:text-left lg:col-start-1 lg:row-start-1">
              <p class="text-[#ff1516] tracking-[0.3em] uppercase text-xs mb-4">Comparison</p>
              <h1 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-[2.75rem] xl:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white leading-[1.08] text-balance">
                Lamborghini Huracán STO vs EVO vs EVO Spyder: which to rent in Miami
              </h1>
              <p class="text-white/65 text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed mt-5">
                Renting a Lamborghini Huracán in Miami? Here are the STO, EVO and EVO Spyder side by side — price, power, deposit and age — and why the STO is the one we recommend.
              </p>
            </div>

            <figure class="mt-8 lg:mt-0 lg:col-start-2 lg:row-start-1 lg:row-span-2 lg:self-center">
              <img
                src={heroSrc}
                srcset={heroSrcSet}
                sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 520px, 100vw"
                width="760"
                height="507"
                alt={heroAlt}
                fetchpriority="high"
                decoding="async"
                class="w-full h-auto rounded-2xl"
              />
              <figcaption class="text-white/45 text-xs mt-3 text-center lg:text-left">
                Our Huracán STO, {usd(sto.price)} a day.
              </figcaption>
            </figure>

            <div class="text-center lg:text-left lg:col-start-1 lg:row-start-2 lg:self-end">
              <div class="mt-8 lg:mt-7 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center lg:justify-start gap-x-5 gap-y-2 text-sm text-white/60">
                <span>By <a href="/about" class="text-white underline decoration-white/30 hover:decoration-white">Robert Comella</a>, founder</span>
                <span aria-hidden="true" class="text-white/25">|</span>
                <span><time datetime={PUBLISHED_ISO}>{published}</time> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> Updated <time datetime={UPDATED_ISO}>{updated}</time></span>
                <span aria-hidden="true" class="text-white/25">|</span>
                <span>{readingMinutes} min read</span>
              </div>

              <div class="mt-6 flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3 max-w-md mx-auto lg:mx-0">
                {/* Primary hero CTA goes to the STO car page (owner, 15 Nov 2026),
                    not WhatsApp: the page has the photos, terms and booking card.
                    No WhatsApp dot, since this is no longer a WhatsApp link. */}
                <a href={`/cars/${sto.slug}`} data-cta="blog_hero"
                   class="flex-1 inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 min-h-[48px] bg-white text-black px-7 py-4 rounded-full font-semibold whitespace-nowrap hover:bg-[#ff1516] transition">
                  Book STO
                </a>
                <a href={telHref} data-cta="blog_hero" data-call-inline
                   class="flex-1 inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-[48px] border border-white/25 text-white px-7 py-4 rounded-full font-medium hover:border-[#e00e10] hover:text-[#e00e10] transition">
                  Call {business.phoneDisplayShort}
                </a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </header>

    <article>
      <div class="bg-white text-[#0a0a0a] py-12 md:py-16">
        <div class="max-w-[1140px] mx-auto px-5 md:px-8">

          <div class="not-prose mb-10 md:mb-14 rounded-2xl border border-[#e00e10]/20 bg-[#fff7f7] p-6 md:p-8 max-w-3xl">
            <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#e00e10] font-semibold mb-3">Short answer</p>
            <p class="text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed">
              <strong>
                Rent the Huracán STO if the drive is the point: {sto.power} hp, {sto.zeroToSixty} to 60 and the race-car body, for {usd(sto.price)} a day. Rent the EVO at {usd(evo.price)} if you want the same V10 with a softer ride, and the EVO Spyder at {usd(spyder.price)} if the roof has to come off.
              </strong>
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="lg:grid lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,260px)_minmax(0,1fr)] lg:gap-14 xl:gap-20">
            <aside class="mb-10 lg:mb-0">
              <nav aria-label="Table of contents" class="not-prose lg:sticky lg:top-28 rounded-2xl border border-black/10 bg-[#fafafa] p-6">
                <h2 class="font-display text-base font-bold mb-3">On this page</h2>
                <ol class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-1 gap-x-6 gap-y-2.5 text-sm">
                  {toc.map((t, i) => (
                    <li>
                      <a href={`#${t.id}`} class="text-[#e00e10] hover:underline">
                        <span class="text-black/60 tabular-nums mr-1">{i + 1}.</span>{t.label}
                      </a>
                    </li>
                  ))}
                </ol>
              </nav>
            </aside>

            <div class="prose prose-neutral max-w-none prose-headings:font-display prose-headings:scroll-mt-28 prose-a:text-[#e00e10] prose-a:underline prose-a:decoration-[#e00e10]/40 prose-a:underline-offset-2 hover:prose-a:decoration-[#e00e10] prose-table:text-sm prose-h2:mt-12 prose-h2:pt-8 prose-h2:border-t prose-h2:border-black/10 first:prose-h2:mt-0 first:prose-h2:pt-0 first:prose-h2:border-0">

        <p>
          A Lamborghini in Miami is roughly a Honda anywhere else. The one people still turn around for is the one with a wing.
        </p>

        <p>
          We rent three Huracáns, and they are less alike than the name suggests. Which one to book
          depends on what the rental is for. For most people who want a Lamborghini in Miami because
          they want to drive one, it is the STO, and this guide explains why — along with the cases
          where we would point you at the cheaper car instead.
        </p>

        <h2 id="what-they-share">What all three Huracáns share</h2>

        <p>
          Start with what is the same, because it is more than people expect. All three use the
          naturally aspirated 5.2-litre V10, and all three send their power to the rear wheels only.
          None of them has a hybrid system or an electric mode, so none of them leaves quietly. Every
          one is strictly a two-seater with a small front trunk and no rear cargo space.
        </p>

        <p>
          That means the decision is not about the engine note or the badge. It is about three things:
          how the car rides, whether it has a roof you can take off, and how far it has been taken
          toward the race track. On that last one, the gap between the STO and the other two is wide.
        </p>

        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>&nbsp;</th><th>Huracán STO</th><th>Huracán EVO</th><th>EVO Spyder</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Per day</td><td><strong>{usd(sto.price)}</strong></td><td><strong>{usd(evo.price)}</strong></td><td><strong>{usd(spyder.price)}</strong></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Power</td><td>{sto.power} hp</td><td>{evo.power} hp</td><td>{spyder.power} hp</td></tr>
            <tr><td>0–60</td><td>{sto.zeroToSixty}</td><td>{evo.zeroToSixty}</td><td>{spyder.zeroToSixty}</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Roof</td><td>Coupe</td><td>Coupe</td><td>Soft top</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Seats</td><td>{sto.seats}</td><td>{evo.seats}</td><td>{spyder.seats}</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Deposit</td><td>{sto.deposit.display}</td><td>{evo.deposit.display}</td><td>{spyder.deposit.display}</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Minimum age</td><td>{sto.minimumAge}+</td><td>{evo.minimumAge}+</td><td>{spyder.minimumAge}+</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Per day, 3+ days</td><td>{usd(threeDay(sto))}</td><td>{usd(threeDay(evo))}</td><td>{usd(threeDay(spyder))}</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Per day, 7+ days</td><td>{usd(week(sto))}</td><td>{usd(week(evo))}</td><td>{usd(week(spyder))}</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <h2 id="sto-vs-evo">What the Huracán STO adds over the EVO</h2>

        <p>
          STO stands for Super Trofeo Omologata: the road-legal version of the car Lamborghini races in
          its own one-make series. You can see it before you hear it. The roof scoop feeds the engine,
          the rear wing is there for downforce rather than decoration, and most of the body panels are
          carbon fibre. Lamborghini's own <a href="https://www.lamborghini.com/en-en/history/huracan-sto" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">history of the Huracán STO</a> sets out what was carried over from the race car.
        </p>

        <p>
          On the spec sheet the STO makes {sto.power} hp against the EVO's {evo.power}, {hpGap} more,
          and gets to 60 in {sto.zeroToSixty} against {evo.zeroToSixty}. Those figures undersell it. What
          you notice on the road is how directly the car answers the steering and how firmly it sits
          down, and that is the part no 0–60 time captures. The independent <a href="https://www.carexpert.com.au/car-reviews/2022-lamborghini-huracan-sto-review" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CarExpert review of the STO</a> covers the carbon-ceramic brakes and the aero in more depth than we need to here.
        </p>

        <p>
          On the steering wheel sits a switch with three modes: STO for the road, Trofeo for the track
          and Pioggia for rain. In Miami you will use the first and, in summer, occasionally the third.
        </p>

        <figure class="not-prose my-10">
          <img
            src={bodySrc}
            srcset={bodySrcSet}
            sizes="(min-width: 1140px) 760px, 100vw"
            width="1000"
            height="747"
            alt={bodyAlt}
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            class="w-full h-auto rounded-2xl"
          />
          <figcaption class="text-black/60 text-sm mt-3">The roof scoop and rear wing are what separate the STO from every other Huracán, and both are working parts.</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <p>
          The price of all that is {usd(stoOverEvo)} a day over the EVO. For a car that is genuinely a
          different machine rather than the same one in a louder color, we think it is the easiest
          premium in the fleet to justify. A wing on a Huracán is not subtle, and it is not meant to be.
        </p>

        <h2 id="evo-vs-spyder">Huracán EVO vs EVO Spyder: the roof is the whole difference</h2>

        <p>
          If you have already decided against the STO, the choice between the EVO and the EVO Spyder is
          simpler. Same {evo.power} hp V10, same two seats, same small front trunk. The Spyder costs
          {' '}{usd(spyderOverEvo)} a day more and gives you a soft top that folds away; the EVO coupe is
          the slightly quicker of the two, at {evo.zeroToSixty} to 60 against the Spyder's {spyder.zeroToSixty}.
        </p>

        <p>
          Take the Spyder if the plan is Ocean Drive in the evening and you want the V10 unfiltered. Take
          the EVO if you would rather have a fixed roof over you in August and the lower rate. Neither choice is wrong. Our <a href={`/cars/${spyder.slug}`}>Huracán EVO Spyder rental page</a> has the full detail on the roof.
        </p>

        <h2 id="when-not-the-sto">When the EVO or the Spyder is the better call</h2>

        <p>
          We recommend the cheaper car when it is genuinely the better fit, and with the Huracáns there
          are four cases where it is.
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li><strong>You are under {sto.minimumAge}.</strong> The STO is {sto.minimumAge}+; the EVO and the Spyder are {evo.minimumAge}+. That settles it.</li>
          <li><strong>The deposit matters.</strong> The STO takes {sto.deposit.display}, the EVO and Spyder {evo.deposit.display}. All three are refundable, but the hold is real money for the length of the rental.</li>
          <li><strong>Comfort comes first.</strong> The STO is set up for a track and rides firmly over rough Miami streets. If most of the booking is a long cruise, the <a href={`/cars/${evo.slug}`}>Huracán EVO</a> is the more relaxed car.</li>
          <li><strong>You want the roof down.</strong> Only the Spyder does that, and it costs {usd(stoOverSpyder)} a day less than the STO.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          Outside those four, we would book the STO. The difference in experience is larger than the
          difference in price.
        </p>

        <figure class="not-prose my-10 rounded-2xl border border-black/10 bg-[#fafafa] p-6">
          <blockquote class="text-[#0a0a0a]/80 leading-relaxed">
            <p>“{testimonial.text}”</p>
          </blockquote>
          <figcaption class="mt-4 text-sm text-[#0a0a0a]/60">
            <span class="text-[#e00e10]" aria-hidden="true">★★★★★</span>
            <span class="font-semibold text-[#0a0a0a]"> {testimonial.name}</span> — verified Google review
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <h2 id="terms">Deposit, age and mileage, side by side</h2>

        <p>
          The terms are published and the same for everyone, so here they are without the sales voice.
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li><strong>Deposit:</strong> {sto.deposit.display} on the STO, {evo.deposit.display} on the EVO and the Spyder. Refundable after the car is inspected on return.</li>
          <li><strong>Minimum age:</strong> {sto.minimumAge} for the STO, {evo.minimumAge} for the EVO and the Spyder, with a valid license.</li>
          <li><strong>Insurance:</strong> {insurance.summary}</li>
          <li><strong>Mileage:</strong> {perDay} miles a day on all three, pooled across the rental.</li>
          <li><strong>Taxes and fees:</strong> {taxPct}% of the rental, after any multi-day rate.</li>
          <li><strong>Cancellation:</strong> {cancellation.summary}</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          One position worth stating: mileage should be pooled, not capped by the day. {perDay} miles a
          day on a three-day booking is {perDay * 3} miles in total, spendable however you like. Drive
          the STO up the coast on day one and leave it parked on day two, and you are still inside the
          allowance. A daily cap that resets at midnight is a worse deal at the same headline price, and
          it is exactly the wrong rule for a car people rent in order to drive.
        </p>

        <h2 id="our-pick">Why we would put you in the STO</h2>

        <p>
          Most people renting a Huracán in Miami are not choosing transport. They are choosing a day, or a
          weekend, that they will remember for the car. On that measure the STO is the strongest of the
          three by a distance: it is the one that feels and looks unlike anything else on the road, and it
          is the one the people around you will recognize as something different.
        </p>

        <p>
          The EVO is an excellent car and we rent it happily. But if you have already decided to spend a
          Lamborghini day in Miami, the extra {usd(stoOverEvo)} is what turns it from a nice car into the
          car you came for. Everything on the <a href={`/cars/${sto.slug}`}>Huracán STO rental page</a> — photos, rates and availability — is one tap away, and our wider guide to <a href="/lamborghini-rental-miami">Lamborghini rental in Miami</a> covers the Urus as well.
        </p>

        <h2 id="faq">Common questions</h2>

        {faqs.map((f) => (
